A||N||9||Gottico||Drivetrain problems !!New info!!||||9||
Z||000000||Gottico||11-10-2000||11:17 PM||||88’ Formula. Ok, trans mount done correctly this time. Disconnected Tach Filter. Started her up…. Ran good. Took her for a ride… Ran great… Drove about 6 blocks… then it started again… No backfires this time… just shuttering and running like crap….  Seems like when it got nice and warm, it started running bad. Remembered someone saying that a bad coolant sensor could also be the culprit… Disconnected sensor… no effect. Pushed home…. Anyone know a good chiropractor??? I reconnected the tach filter and coolant sensor since it doesn’t seem to be one of them. However, my tach is a little jumpy. I would hook up my code scanner but it’s out on loan to a friend. I’m not sure that would produce the problem though, since it didn’t find anything before… <P>Seems like when it gets warned up, it starts to run like crap… Any ideas???<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||fiero56||11-10-2000||11:18 PM||||Sounds heat related. If it were mine, I would try a different ignition module.<P>MAP sensor is also possible culprit.<P><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||MoneypitGT||11-11-2000||12:07 AM||||Ignition module (inside dist. cap)most definatley. Had that problem on two different cars. Ran great till it warmed up, then forget it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-11-2000||02:57 PM||||While you're in the area, might want to inspect the EGR tube for leaks, and make sure its heat blankie is still in good shape.<P>If the distributor is being heated up by a leaky and/or unshielded EGR tube, the new ignition module probably won't live as long as it should. ||||reg||4
Z||000004||88formula||11-11-2000||03:16 PM||||Try this simple test and you will know for sure that you have a hot ignition related problem or other hot component related problem. If your car runs fine when it’s cold than get a heat gun or hair dryer and heat up the ignition module but not too much, just enough to simulate a hot engine. Try to start the car and see what happens with the engine and everything else cold. If it runs fine than shut it down so the engine doesn't warm up and try this with the coil. If nothing happens than try the computer. Keep doing this until you find the culprit and you will find it.<P>Good luck and let me know what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gottico||11-11-2000||05:49 PM||||Ok, I'm pretty sure it's a heat related problem... It runs great when cold, but when it starts getting warmed up, that's when it all goes to hell... And it gets worse the warmer it gets... I noticed that the distribitor and wires were kinda hot on the last run... On my way to get a new Ignition module then I'll go from there and check the EGR tube...||||reg||3
Z||000006||Gottico||11-11-2000||07:26 PM||||Got code scanner back.... getting all 12's (no stored codes) so hopefully it's the module. Stay tuned... install tomorrow...||||reg||10
Z||000007||88formula||11-12-2000||12:04 AM||||Why don't you try the test I gave you before you waste your money on a part that may not be defective? Diagnose the thing; don't just start replacing parts until you find the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||11-12-2000||10:15 AM||||You can also just take the ig. module to AutoZone and they will test it for free.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gottico||11-12-2000||06:18 PM||||Why not test... I don't own a hair dryer... The code scanner would pick problems with the sensors and it has nothing, Timing is correct, MAP sensor reading good, and I've tested with all the tools I have... Only thing I have left is to tear the engine down... I've narrowed it down to the coil and the module... Module was $11-Hair dryer is $15 ||||reg||1
